## Re-verified premise: attempt-1's defect is fixed

Attempt 1 FAIL: `math.Round(v*100)` decided the differ/same branch while
`FormatMoney` (`%.2f`) rendered the figures — two independent roundings that
disagreed at half-cent boundaries (7639.035/7639.04 → "the same" over two
different displayed figures).

Code at 1405372 (`populateSpendingRowPlanEvidence`,
handlers_spending_optimizer.go:524-542):
  base := budgettemplates.FormatMoney(candidate.BaseMonthlyLivingExpenses)
  start := budgettemplates.FormatMoney(candidate.StartingMonthlyLivingReal)
  if base != start { ...differ... } else { ...same... }
The branch is now decided on the SAME two rendered strings shown to the
user — this is tautologically self-consistent (wording can never contradict
the two displayed figures), eliminating the whole defect class, not just
the one boundary.

