## Verdict
PASS on (a)-(e). The attempt-1 defect (rounding drift between the
comparison and the displayed strings) is eliminated by construction — the
branch decision now reads the same two rendered strings the user sees, so
the wording can never contradict the figures. Reproduced the exact
attempt-1 boundary plus 9 additional probes (including a $1M straddle and a
negative sub-cent corner) against the real code: all self-consistent.
Mutation check confirms the shipped test would catch a regression back to
the old defect. The one adjacent surface still using a second formatter
(`spendingAppliedAnnouncement`) is unchanged by this diff and out of CF1's
manifest — carried forward as an observation, not a FAIL ground.
